<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	Count badge shown over the HUD diplomacy button's bottom-right corner.
	Based on vanilla hud_campaign.twui.xml > label_missions_count (same image, size and
	font) without its context callbacks. Created under faction_buttons_docker (not inside
	the diplomacy button, whose StatePropagatorCallback forces its own state on its
	children) and positioned from script, so it has no docking here.

	qdi_badge        the disc: interactive (tooltip = deal list, click = open Quick Deal),
	                 single state.
	qdi_badge_glow   the brighter disc (badge_hover.png), visible only while the mouse is
	                 over qdi_badge. Same mechanism as vanilla buttons' hover flame
	                 (templates/square_large_text_button.twui.xml > button_flame): a
	                 ContextVisibilitySetter on self.ParentContext.IsMouseOver, evaluated by
	                 the engine. The badge doesn't switch hover states by itself, and the game
	                 sends no ComponentMouseOn/Off for it.
	qdi_badge_count  the number, drawn on top of the glow; text set from script.
	Both children are non-interactive so the mouse reaches qdi_badge.
-->
